course: dictionary
lesson: 474
title: Arrow: a stick, a sign, a key
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An arrow is a thin straight stick with a sharp point, shot from a bow. The word can mean other things too, so look at the words around it. «Follow the arrows to the exit» tells you the arrows are signs, because you follow them with your eyes and feet, not with a bow.
explain: Other clues help as well. «Press the arrow key to move left» means the arrow is a key on a keyboard. «Straight as an arrow» is an old saying meaning very straight. Each time, ask which meaning fits and swap it into the sentence to check.
explain: In a diagram, arrows show direction. «The arrows in a food chain point from the thing eaten to the thing that eats it.» Here the arrows are signs that show which way food passes, so the clue is the word diagram, not a bow.
fact: An arrow is a thin straight stick with a sharp point at the front and feathers at the back, shot from a bow.
fact: An arrow can also be a sign, shaped like this (→), that points to show a direction or where to look.
fact: An arrow can be a key on a keyboard or screen that moves something when you press it.
fact: «Straight as an arrow» means very straight.
fact: In a food chain, arrows point from food to eater: grass, rabbit, fox.
exercise: «Follow the arrows to the fire exit.» What does arrow mean here? | *A sign that points the way | A thin stick shot from a bow | A sharp point on a rock | A key on a keyboard
exercise: «Press the arrow key to move the character left.» What is the arrow? | *A key on a keyboard shaped like an arrow | A feathered stick shot from a bow | A sign for a one-way street | A pointed piece of metal
exercise: In the food chain grass, rabbit, fox, which way do the arrows point? | Nowhere, they are just decoration | Up into the sky | From the fox back to the grass | *From the thing eaten to the thing that eats it
test: «Robin Hood took aim and let his arrow fly.» What is an arrow here? | *A thin stick with a sharp point, shot from a bow | A sign showing the way out | A key on a keyboard | A line on a number line
test: «The tree stood straight as an arrow.» What does straight as an arrow mean? | Very fast | Very loud | *Very straight | Very bendy
exam: «The arrows on the graph show that the line goes on and on.» What do the arrows show? | That the graph is finished | That the line is coloured red | *That the line keeps going without stopping | That the line is broken
